A program's own override of a bodyless component for android renders a
`ui.button`, whose android body reads the `flexShare` context. The components
a build renders are collected before the target's override bodies are swapped
in, so the bodyless `dial` looked empty and the button never joined them:
passContext left its read for InlinePure to splice into the view, and Kotlin's
emitter panicked on a bare `ir.ContextRead` under `--lang go`. The override
body is walked too.

unverifiable out/go/android -- the emitted project consumes a golib.aar produced by a `gomobile bind` step that generation does not perform

-- app.sngl --
import android "sngl:platform/android"
import ui "sngl:ui"

output {
    go {
        android
    }
}

component dial(:value int) ui.node

component dial[android.platform](value) {
    ui.button(text="{value}", @click { value += 1 })
}

component page ui.node {
    var n = 0

    dial(:value=n)
}

ui.window {
    page
}
